From ca49197118f6e39589f8f546dc15ef60fbc92e62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <226450061+logdog2325@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 15:46:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 163/164] XD Netplay: desync fix, Multi team combination and
 trainer models, host Watch only, music names

- CoreTiming: the first slice's downcount uses this boot's overclock factor. It was computed
  from the previous session's (0 in a freshly opened app), so the first boot after opening
  OrreLink ran 20000 cycles off every later boot, and a room mixing fresh and reused windows
  split minutes into a battle. The cpu log line records proc_boot and the first slice.
- Multi: the team combination is no longer pinned to the first option; each battle logs the
  slots and the room chat names the teams (XdNoticeKind::MultiSides, port-1 owner only).
- Multi: every seat wears its own trainer model (staging TID pins and borrowed switch arms,
  GenerateMultiModelLines); solo Multi boots read MultiSoloModels for ports 2-4.
- 1v1: the host can watch. The next two players in line play GBA 1 and GBA 2 from staged
  teams and boot copies (PrepareWatchStart, NetSettings::xd_boot_copies), with their own
  models; the host keeps XD's menus. Teams reset when the host switches; the buffer is sized
  for the joiner to host to joiner route.
- Music named from the game's battle data (Trainer Battle, Cipher Peon Battle, Cipher Admin
  Battle), Gonzap and Hexagon Bros fixed, XD Battle 0 removed (same track as Battle Sim),
  Miror B. Theme and Mt. Battle clouds tested; the Krane model is named for what it shows.
